<workout_file><author>mywhooshinfo.com</author><name>2023 TDF George Bennett - Climbing</name><description>George Bennett, a seasoned General Classification rider, understands the significance of perfecting his climbing fitness. The workout scheduled for today entails three 10-minute climbs, with every ascent executed at a target cadence.

Like an outdoor climb, the power demanded will escalate for 10 minutes, culminating in 1 minute above the threshold at the climb&#039;s summit.

Assume a bike position as you would during a long climb.</description><sportType>bike</sportType><workout>
<Warmup  Duration="600" PowerLow="0.50449997186661" PowerHigh="0.75449997186661"><textevent timeoffset="60" message="Welcome to George Bennett&#039;s Grand Tour workout."/><textevent timeoffset="120" message="George has a successful stage racing career himself."/><textevent timeoffset="180" message="But he is also one of Pogacar&#039;s trusted domestiques."/><textevent timeoffset="240" message="To be competitive in stage racing, Bennett knows the importance of improving his climbing fitness."/><textevent timeoffset="300" message="Today we are going to experience the type of training Bennett completes to hit the start of a Grand Tour race, in top form."/><textevent timeoffset="360" message="Today we will complete 3, ten-minute climbs."/><textevent timeoffset="420" message="But as the climb continues, we increase the power."/><textevent timeoffset="480" message="To simulate the demands of climbing, we have a target cadence for each step of the climb."/></Warmup>
<SteadyState  Duration="60" Power="0.55449998378754"><textevent timeoffset="20" message="Here we go. Into the first climb."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Cadence="85" Duration="300" Power="0.80449998378754"><textevent timeoffset="20" message="Hit the target cadence of 85rpm and let the smart trainer adjust the power."/><textevent timeoffset="80" message="Being in zone 3, this effort should feel relatively comfortable for you."/><textevent timeoffset="140" message="Just like in a Tour de France climb, we are going to increase the intensity as we near the summit."/><textevent timeoffset="200" message="It&#039;s on these early slopes that Bennett controls the pace at the front of the peloton."/><textevent timeoffset="260" message="It&#039;s time to up the effort as we approach halfway."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Cadence="85" Duration="240" Power="0.95450001955032"><textevent timeoffset="20" message="Hit the target cadence of 85rpm and let the smart trainer adjust the power."/><textevent timeoffset="80" message="We are in zone 4 now. The climbing begins to take its toll."/><textevent timeoffset="140" message="This is where Bennett shows his strength by riding a solid effort on the front."/><textevent timeoffset="190" message="Relax your hands on the bars. Focus on maintaining a good climbing position."/><textevent timeoffset="210" message="To be well positioned for the descent, it&#039;s time to increase the pace."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Cadence="85" Duration="60" Power="1.0544999837875"><textevent timeoffset="10" message="Just 1 minute in Zone 5 to hold your place at the front of the group."/><textevent timeoffset="50" message="There&#039;s the summit!"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="240" Power="0.55000001192093"><textevent timeoffset="30" message="Grab a drink during this recovery period."/><textevent timeoffset="220" message="This time we are targeting 80rpm on the climb."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Cadence="80" Duration="300" Power="0.80449998378754"><textevent timeoffset="20" message="Hit the target cadence of 80rpm and let the smart trainer adjust the power."/><textevent timeoffset="80" message="Being in zone 3, this effort should feel relatively comfortable for you."/><textevent timeoffset="140" message="Just like in a Tour de France climb, we are going to increase the intensity as we near the summit."/><textevent timeoffset="200" message="Bennett knows the importance of being able to ride multiple climbs at a steady pace in a single stage."/><textevent timeoffset="260" message="This type of training allows him to be good on the first climb. And good on the last climb!"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Cadence="80" Duration="240" Power="0.95450001955032"><textevent timeoffset="20" message="Hit the target cadence of 80rpm and let the smart trainer adjust the power."/><textevent timeoffset="80" message="We are in zone 4 now. The climbing begins to take its toll."/><textevent timeoffset="140" message="This is where Bennett shows his strength by riding a solid effort on the front."/><textevent timeoffset="190" message="Relax your hands on the bars. Focus on maintaining a good climbing position."/><textevent timeoffset="210" message="To be well positioned for the descent, it&#039;s time to increase the pace."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Cadence="80" Duration="60" Power="1.0544999837875"><textevent timeoffset="10" message="Just 1 minute in Zone 5 to hold your place at the front of the group."/><textevent timeoffset="50" message="There&#039;s the summit!"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="240" Power="0.55449998378754"><textevent timeoffset="30" message="Grab a drink during this recovery period."/><textevent timeoffset="220" message="This time, we are targeting 75rpm on the climb."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Cadence="75" Duration="300" Power="0.80449998378754"><textevent timeoffset="20" message="Here we go into the final climb of the day!"/><textevent timeoffset="80" message="Hit the target cadence of 75rpm and let the smart trainer adjust the power."/><textevent timeoffset="140" message="Just like in a Tour de France climb, we are going to increase the intensity as we near the summit."/><textevent timeoffset="200" message="It&#039;s on these early slopes that Bennett controls the pace at the front of the peloton."/><textevent timeoffset="260" message="It&#039;s time to up the effort as we approach halfway."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Cadence="75" Duration="240" Power="0.95450001955032"><textevent timeoffset="20" message="Hit the target cadence of 75rpm and let the smart trainer adjust the power."/><textevent timeoffset="80" message="We are in zone 4 now. The climbing begins to take its toll."/><textevent timeoffset="140" message="This is where Bennett shows his strength by riding a solid effort on the front."/><textevent timeoffset="190" message="Relax your hands on the bars. Focus on maintaining a good climbing position."/><textevent timeoffset="210" message="To be well positioned for the descent, it&#039;s time to increase the pace."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Cadence="75" Duration="60" Power="1.0544999837875"><textevent timeoffset="10" message="Just 1 minute in Zone 5 to hold your place at the front of the group."/><textevent timeoffset="50" message="There&#039;s the summit!"/></SteadyState>
<Cooldown  Duration="300" PowerLow="0.50449997186661" PowerHigh="0.40450000762939"><textevent timeoffset="30" message="Well done. That completes the work for today."/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="Now we have a nice long recovery period to spin the legs out a little."/><textevent timeoffset="150" message="We hope you have enjoyed completing this Grand Tour session from George Bennett."/><textevent timeoffset="210" message="Bennett certainly knows how to bring himself into good form for a Grand Tour."/><textevent timeoffset="240" message="His long career is testament to that."/><textevent timeoffset="280" message="We hope to see you in the other UAE Team Emirates Grand Tour workouts."/></Cooldown>
</workout></workout_file>